  "narrative": "Interim synthesis report, iteration 8. I reassessed all due evidence and the new validation results. The two robust dataset-specific associations remain unchanged and remain the central supported findings. First, feature_050=1 versus feature_050=0 is associated with a very large stronger-dependency shift in outcome_001. Because the registered direction was -1, the signed estimates are positive: R56 discovery +0.784 [0.765, 0.803] and independent validation R76 +0.805 [0.774, 0.836]. With an approximate outcome_001 10% absolute-mean threshold near 0.0415, both lower bounds are far above clinical significance. I therefore keep H88 accepted and closed. Second, feature_027=1 versus 0 remains associated with a very large positive outcome_014 shift, with validated R14/R26 lower bounds far above the outcome_014 threshold near 0.0093. These are associations within the supplied dataset and defined strata, not causal or externally generalizable claims.\n\nAmong due reassessments, H17 remains rejected: the feature_050 effect on outcome_003 in the registered negative-dependency direction was not supported by discovery or validation. R52 and R77 are both small and not interval-supported for a clinically meaningful stronger-dependency effect against the approximate outcome_003 threshold near 0.0253. H103 is now rejected: the feature_065 negative-direction outcome_001 association was only weakly positive in discovery and opposite in validation, with the validation estimate -0.018 [-0.076, 0.040] providing no support against the outcome_001 threshold. H127 is rejected. Its discovery evidence R89 was clinically suggestive in the signed negative direction (+0.035, lower bound -0.001), but the independent validation R102 was in the opposite signed direction (-0.005 [-0.061, 0.051]) and is not supportive. This contradiction argues against accepting an overall negative feature_042 association on outcome_014. The separate controlled feature_027=0 test, H140, remains pending and may reveal whether any effect is stratum-specific rather than confounded by the dominant feature_027 outcome_014 marker.\n\nThe secondary outcome_014 candidates remain unresolved rather than accepted. H126, feature_045 in the positive raw direction, has R88 +0.0218 [-0.0153, 0.0590], and H128, feature_065 in the negative raw direction, has R75 +0.0319 [-0.0074, 0.0711]. Both point estimates exceed the small outcome_014 threshold, but neither discovery lower bound clears clinical significance, and the failure of H127 validation warns against accepting near-threshold unstratified effects. I therefore keep H126 and H128 active and propose controlled feature_027=0 screens for feature_045 and feature_065. The feature_054 result is scientifically interesting but not accepted. H129 gives a positive raw level_002 versus level_001 estimate within feature_050=0, while H130 gives a negative raw estimate within feature_050=1; the sign-corrected H138 is clinically suggestive in magnitude but its signed lower bound is only 0.0003, far below the 0.0093 threshold. This heterogeneity motivates feature_050-interaction follow-up and controlled feature_027=0 strata, not acceptance. Next I will prioritize analysis of H140 and the newly proposed controlled screens, and also the feature_054 stratum-controlled claims. If a controlled candidate converges or its lower bound crosses the relevant clinical threshold, the next validation request should target the best controlled or sign-corrected candidate. Otherwise these secondary axes should be closed as dataset-specific noise or imprecision.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 8 synthesis. Due validations assessed: H88 accepted (outcome_001 feature_050 negative direction: discovery +0.784, validation +0.805, threshold ~0.0415). H17 rejected (outcome_003 feature_050 negative direction: discovery/validation not clinically supported, threshold ~0.0253). H103 rejected (outcome_001 feature_065: discovery weak positive signed +0.0089, validation opposite -0.018, threshold ~0.0415). H127 rejected (outcome_014 feature_042 negative direction: discovery signed +0.035 lower -0.001; validation opposite signed -0.005 wide, inconsistent). Central accepted associations unchanged: feature_027=1 for outcome_014 positive shift, validated; feature_050=1 for outcome_001 negative dependency shift, validated. All are dataset-specific associations, not causal/generalizable. Secondary candidates: feature_045 positive R88 +0.0218 [-0.0153,0.0590] unresolved active; feature_065 negative R75 +0.0319 [-0.0074,0.0711] unresolved active; feature_054 heterogeneity: R90 positive within feature_050=0 +0.0281 [-0.0117,0.0680] unresolved; R91 negative within feature_050=1, sign-corrected H138 lower +0.0003 not clinically accepted. Proposed controlled feature_027=0 tests for feature_045/065 and feature_050/feature_027 controlled feature_054 tests. Existing H140 (feature_042 within feature_027=0) pending. Next analyze should select H140 and new controlled tests plus feature_054 interaction. Future validation priority: only a candidate with controlled convergence or interval above 10% threshold; likely best among current unvalidated candidates if controlled results are supportive: feature_065 outcome_014 negative, feature_045 outcome_014 positive, or feature_054 feature_050 interaction."
